🔹 What is CloudFront?

CloudFront is AWS’s global Content Delivery Network (CDN). 
Amazon Web Services, Inc.
+1

It uses a worldwide network of Edge Locations (POPs), so your end-users receive content from the nearest edge, reducing latency. 
Amazon Web Services, Inc.
+1

The typical architecture:

End User → CloudFront Edge Location → Origin (S3 / EC2 / ALB)  


If content is already cached at the edge, CloudFront serves it immediately; otherwise, it fetches from the origin. 
Amazon Web Services, Inc.
+1

🔹 Why use CloudFront?

Faster content delivery worldwide

Lower latency and faster page load

Offload origin resources (EC2/S3)

Supports HTTPS, custom SSL/TLS, custom domains

Integration with AWS services: S3, ALB, Lambda@Edge, WAF

Edge caching helps scale traffic spikes

🔹 Example: Create first distribution using EC2 instance as origin

Step-by-step:

Launch your EC2 instance (e.g., web server with nginx or apache) in a region. Ensure its security group allows HTTP/HTTPS from CloudFront or any.

In AWS Console → CloudFront → Create Distribution

Choose Web distribution (for HTTP/HTTPS content).

Origin domain name: select your EC2 instance (or enter custom origin, e.g., ec2-xxx.compute.amazonaws.com).

Origin protocol policy: HTTP only / HTTPS only / Match viewer.

Default cache behavior: Path pattern /*, Viewer protocol policy: Redirect HTTP to HTTPS (recommended).

Distribution settings: Alternate domain names (CNAME) if using custom domain, SSL certificate (via AWS Certificate Manager), Logging etc.

After creation, note the Domain Name something like: d123abcd4e.cloudfront.net

Point your DNS (Route 53 or other) CNAME to this domain if you use custom domain.

Test: Access the CloudFront domain → you should see the content served by EC2, and subsequent requests served from nearest edge location (cache hit).

Monitor: Check CloudFront metrics, cache hit/miss, X-Cache response header: “Hit from CloudFront” vs “Miss from CloudFront”.

🔹 Key Concepts

Distribution: A collection of edge locations + settings for content delivery.

Origin: The source of content (S3 bucket, EC2 instance, ALB, custom HTTP server).

Cache Behavior: Path patterns and settings (TTL, cookies, query strings) for caching.

Edge Location: Global PoP where content is cached for quick access.

🔹 Best Practices

Use HTTPS between viewer and CloudFront, and optionally between CloudFront and origin.

Use custom domain + SSL certificate for branding.

Set long TTLs for static assets; invalidate when you update files.

Monitor cache hit ratio; optimize origin offload.

Use Origin Shield for further caching efficiency (for high traffic).

Enable logging and capture X-Cache header.

Use WAF to protect origins from malicious traffic.


✅ 1. What is Cache Expiry in CloudFront?

CloudFront world-wide edge location वर तुमचा data/cache store करतो.
पण तो cached data कायम ठेवत नाही — त्याचा एक expiry time (TTL) असतो.

🔸 TTL म्हणजे Time to Live

CloudFront cached object किती वेळापर्यंत ठेवेल ते TTL सांगतो.

TTL चे तीन type:
TTL Type	Meaning
Minimum TTL	CloudFront किमान इतका वेळ तरी object cache मध्ये ठेवेल
Maximum TTL	CloudFront यापेक्षा जास्त वेळ object ठेवणार नाही
Default TTL	Default lifetime जर origin कडून “Cache-Control header” नसला तर
🧠 2. TTL कसे Work करतो? (Real Example)
Scenario:

तुमचे API (/api/v1/products) servers वर updated झाले.

Without TTL Cache:
CloudFront वारंवार origin (EC2/ALB) कडे request पाठवेल → latency जास्त → cost जास्त.

With Proper TTL:
CloudFront edge वर cached data देईल → fast performance → कमी लागत.

📍 3. Cache Expiry कसे Set करतात?
STEP 1: CloudFront → Behaviors → Edit

तुमच्या API/Website path साठी behavior निवडा.

STEP 2: TTL Values Set करा:

Minimum TTL → 0 sec

Default TTL → 5 sec / 60 sec / 300 sec (API वर अवलंबून)

Maximum TTL → 1 hour किंवा जास्त (static files साठी)

👉 API साठी TTL कमी
👉 Static Website files (HTML, CSS, JS, Images) साठी TTL जास्त

🎯 4. Custom Headers in CloudFront (MOST IMPORTANT)

CloudFront तुम्ही origin (EC2/ALB/S3) कडे request पाठवताना काही headers automatically add करू शकतो.

Custom Headers का Use करतात?

✔ Security

कोणत्याही direct EC2 API वर hit करू नये

CloudFront → EC2 communication साठी एक secret header वापरतात

उदा:

X-Secret-Key: Abcd1234


EC2 वर check करता:

if (request.header.x-secret-key != Abcd1234) { BLOCK }


✔ Cache Variation Control

CloudFront मधून region, device, language इत्यादी headers add करता येतात

Example: User-Agent header caching

✔ Debugging

“X-Debug-ID” add करून logs trace करता येतात

🧩 5. Custom Header कसे Add करायचे?
STEP 1: CloudFront → Origin → Edit
STEP 2: Add Custom Header

Example:

Header Name	Header Value
X-CloudFront-Token	my-secret-token-9812

CloudFront आता origin कडे request पाठवताना हा header जोडेल.

🛡️ Real Security Use Case (Interview Favourite)

तुमचा EC2 API publicly open आहे → कोणीही call करू शकतो.

🔒 तुम्ही EC2 Security Group मध्ये rule लावता:

Allow only CloudFront IP ranges

OR, better → Validate custom header

Now तुमचा origin ONLY CloudFront मधून content serve करेल.

🚀 6. Cache Expiry + Custom Header – Project Flow
User → CloudFront

(CloudFront तपासतो की cache मध्ये data आहे?)

If YES → User ला cache मधून response

If NO → CloudFront origin कडे request पाठवतो

Custom header add करतो

Origin response देतो

CloudFront त्याला cache करतो (TTL नुसार)

